This PR addresses a performance issue in the domain statistics calculation where the same keywords array was being iterated multiple times to calculate `mapPackKeywords`, `keywordPositions`, and `KeywordsUpdateDates`.

## Problem

The original implementation performed three separate operations on the keywords array:

```typescript
// 1. Filter and count map pack keywords
domainWithStat.mapPackKeywords = keywords.filter((keyword) => keyword.mapPackTop3 === true).length;

// 2. Sum all keyword positions  
const keywordPositions = keywords.reduce((acc, itm) => (acc + itm.position), 0);

// 3. Build array of update dates (inefficient with array spread)
const KeywordsUpdateDates: number[] = keywords.reduce((acc: number[], itm) => [...acc, new Date(itm.lastUpdated).getTime()], [0]);
```

This resulted in:
- **O(3n) time complexity** due to multiple iterations
- **Inefficient memory usage** from array spread operations (`[...acc, item]`) that create new arrays on each iteration
- **Redundant work** when processing domains with many keywords

## Solution

Replaced the three separate operations with a single, efficient `reduce` that calculates all values in one pass:

```typescript
const { mapPackKeywords, keywordPositions, KeywordsUpdateDates } = keywords.reduce(
  (stats, keyword) => {
    if (keyword.mapPackTop3 === true) {
      stats.mapPackKeywords++;
    }
    stats.keywordPositions += keyword.position;
    stats.KeywordsUpdateDates.push(new Date(keyword.lastUpdated).getTime());
    return stats;
  },
  { mapPackKeywords: 0, keywordPositions: 0, KeywordsUpdateDates: [0] as number[] },
);
```

## Performance Benefits

- **Reduced time complexity** from O(3n) to O(n)
- **Eliminated expensive array spread operations** that were creating new arrays on each iteration
- **Single pass** through the keywords data instead of three separate iterations
- **Maintains identical functionality** with 100% backward compatibility

## Testing

- All existing tests continue to pass (346/346)
- Added comprehensive test coverage including edge cases
- Verified identical behavior for various keyword combinations
- Confirmed build and linting remain clean

This optimization provides significant performance improvements for domains with large numbers of keywords while maintaining complete functional compatibility.

Fixes #419.

